WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.605
Might the diabetes drug Metformin
have an anti-aging effect?

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:11.299
Check out this 3-video series to see
what the science says.

00:00:11.423 --> 00:00:18.092
"Does Metformin Work
as a Life-Extension Drug?"

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.680
The noxious weed goat's rue

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.600
was widely used
as an herbal medicine

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.200
back in the Middle Ages for
thirst and frequent urination,

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.600
what we now know of
as a cardinal symptom

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:29.960
and sign of diabetes.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.800
The plant produces
a mitochondrial poison

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.800
known as galegine.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:38.440
One can imagine
how this could help discourage

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:39.880
grazing herbivores,

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:42.080
but why would crippling
mitochondrial function

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:44.640
help with diabetes?

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.520
Well, if you got the dose
just right,

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.040
you could impair
energy production just enough

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.800
to spring AMPK into action.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:53.480
AMPK would then dial down

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.480
the liver's
energy-intensive process

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:59.160
of sugar production,
and blood sugars would fall.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:02.640
Galegine proved too toxic
for use in humans

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.280
(and presumably goats)

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:08.120
but was tweaked
into a milder form in the 1950s.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:10.360
That's the origin story
of metformin,

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:12.360
now, even 60+ years later

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:16.640
the most widely prescribed
diabetes drug in the world.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:20.360
Sold originally as Glucophage
(meaning "sugar eater"),

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:22.240
metformin is
now prescribed annually

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:25.720
more than 90 million times
in the U.S. alone.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:28.400
Despite all the strides
in biotechnology,

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.400
Big Pharma has yet
to come up with a safer,

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.040
more effective
first-line treatment

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:34.840
for type 2 diabetes
than a drug

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:37.480
that retails
at pennies per pill.

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:41.160
Ramping up AMPK
isn't all that metformin does

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:43.080
(for example, it also appears
to foster the growth

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:44.960
of good bacteria
in the gut).

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.800
But the AMPK boost alone
would be expected

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:50.160
to have
wide-ranging health effects.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:53.920
Remember, AMPK is activated
when resources are scarce;

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:56.000
so, it causes the body
to hunker down

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.560
into energy-conservation mode

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:00.600
and put the brakes
on new construction projects.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.080
So, no more making excess
blood sugar or cholesterol.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:06.680
Time to start tapping
into the larder.

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:09.480
And, indeed, metformin doesn't
just lower sugars in the blood

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:11.360
but cholesterol and body fat.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:14.600
And shutting down
the excess synthesis of proteins

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:17.680
can also have health benefits.

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:21.600
Fibrosis is the accumulation
of scar tissue

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.960
in response
to an inflammatory insult.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:26.640
As a transient,
localized phenomenon,

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:30.000
fibrosis helps heal wounds
and repair damaged tissue,

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.640
but in response to the systemic
inflammation of aging,

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:36.240
surplus scar tissue
can build up in our heart,

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.640
liver, kidneys, and lungs.

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:42.360
Excess fibrosis is estimated
to contribute to 45 percent

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.560
of all death
in the United States.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:48.120
But AMPK switches the body
into miser mode,

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:49.560
shrinking the energy budget

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.320
for such superfluous activities

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:54.840
and ratchets down
fibrotic processes.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:58.680
The AMPK priorities shift
from growth to preservation

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:01.960
might also be expected
to slow cancer progression.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:04.440
Based on dozens
of observational studies

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:07.400
involving tens of thousands
of diabetic cancer patients,

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:10.080
those on metformin
did indeed experience

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.040
a significant
survival advantage,

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:15.080
correlating with
a 26 percent decreased risk

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:17.080
of dying from cancer.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:20.080
No wonder there are
more than 100 ongoing studies

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:23.360
to put metformin
to the test against cancer.

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:26.160
As the director of Harvard's
Cancer Center put it,

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.160
"Metformin may have
already saved more people

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:33.760
from cancer deaths
than any drug in history."

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:36.200
If AMPK plays such a key role

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.920
in the aging process,

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.200
and metformin boosts AMPK,

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.800
can metformin slow aging

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:43.960
and lengthen lifespans?

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:45.840
It certainly can
in some species.

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:48.160
C. elegans worms fed metformin

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:49.640
maintained a youthful state

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:52.240
and can exhibit
a nearly 40 percent increase

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:53.840
in average survival.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.160
Interfere with
the AMPK pathway, though,

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.720
and this
lifespan extension disappears,

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:00.560
confirming the role of AMPK

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:04.080
in metformin's
anti-aging effects.

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.400
Metformin also improves

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:08.080
the healthspans
and lifespans of mice,

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.480
but failed to extend
the lives of rats,

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:13.120
calling the pro-longevity
effects of metformin

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:14.720
into question.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.240
The dose they used

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:18.240
(15 times that used in humans)

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:20.120
may have been too high, however,

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.880
and the F344 rats they used

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:24.520
are an inbred strain

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:28.000
(named after the 344th
brother sister mating)

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.360
that are resistant
to the health benefits

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:32.160
of calorie restriction.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.080
Since metformin
acts through AMPK

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.360
as a calorie
restriction mimetic,

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:38.080
it stands to reason
that these animals

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:41.320
may be less prone
to metformin's effects.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:43.480
What about humans?

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:44.720
Unlike other potential

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:47.120
anti-aging drugs
in the pipeline,

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.320
we have the benefit of data

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:50.200
on more than
a million study subjects

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.200
who have been tracked
in metformin trials.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:53.240
And, indeed,

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:54.560
compared to diabetics

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.600
who take drugs
other than metformin,

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:58.520
those on metformin
appear protected

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.680
from age-related
susceptibilities,

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:02.720
like fractures,

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:05.400
or serious infections,

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.440
glaucoma,

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:09.880
and cognitive impairment.

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:10.840
Most importantly,

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:12.280
diabetics who take metformin

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:13.960
live significantly longer

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:16.760
than those taking different
blood sugar-lowering drugs.

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:18.600
Doesn't that prove metformin

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:21.200
is a pro-longevity drug?

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:21.840
No.

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:23.320
For example, maybe metformin

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:25.880
just controlled
their diabetes better.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:28.360
Researchers still found
a survival benefit

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:29.920
for diabetics on metformin

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:33.240
compared to those
as well managed on other drugs,

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:34.360
but maybe the other drugs

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:36.080
were shortening lifespans,

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:39.080
and so, metformin
just looked good in comparison.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:41.720
How could you try
to tease out the effects?

00:05:41.720 --> 00:05:43.240
What if you
compared the lifespans

00:05:43.240 --> 00:05:45.280
of diabetics on metformin

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:48.240
to nondiabetics?

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.320
Now, that's not really
a fair comparison.

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:52.480
Any benefits metformin has

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:54.680
could easily
be outweighed and masked

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:57.560
by the life-limiting
nature of diabetes--

00:05:57.560 --> 00:06:00.280
unless, that is,

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:01.800
the diabetics on metformin

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:04.160
actually lived longer.

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:06.160
Longer than nondiabetics.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:06.680
And,

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:10.480
are you sitting down?

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:13.240
That's exactly
what the research shows.

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:15.440
Diabetics placed on metformin

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:17.320
went on to live longer lives

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:20.240
than those who never
got diabetes in the first place.

00:06:20.240 --> 00:06:22.040
From a longevity standpoint,

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:23.720
it's as if they got lucky

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:25.520
to be diagnosed with diabetes,

00:06:25.520 --> 00:06:29.560
because then, they had access
to this lifespan-enhancing drug.

00:06:29.560 --> 00:06:30.360
So, wait.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:32.840
If metformin is so powerful

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:36.320
as to more than offset
such a dreaded diagnosis,

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:38.920
should everyone
be taking metformin?

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:40.520
What are the downsides?

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:59.400
That's exactly what
I'm gonna be covering next.

